{
  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates whether either lottery contains a 'sure outcome'—that is, an outcome that occurs with 100% probability—and prefers the lottery with such a sure outcome. In this decision problem, neither Lottery A nor Lottery B contains a sure outcome. Lottery A yields -3000 Euros with 90% probability and 0 Euros with 10% probability. Lottery B yields -6000 Euros with 45% probability and 0 Euros with 55% probability. Since no outcome in either lottery occurs with 100% probability, neither lottery has a sure outcome. Therefore, the decision reason would be indifferent between the two lotteries, or possibly not applicable, because its condition (presence of a sure outcome) is not met in either option.",
